            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="0424" n="322" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg322"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/2993a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Reinsch</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-25T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 25, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>British Embassy states it has received instructions to ask us to join in
                    requesting the Chinese Government to remove military Governor [of] Shensi
                    responsible for breach of Armistice. Is this covered by your telegrams March 7,
                    1 p.m.<anchor n="39" xml:id="d328-f1"/> and March 13, 4 p.m. and the
                    Department’s instructions of March 14, 4 p.m. If not what do you think of this
                    proposal?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
